=> floor is a SUM OF POSITIVE totient terms (always >0); the chi_q split is a partition.
   osc/floor stays well below 1 for all q (principal dominates) => the floor never vanishes,
   q-uniformly, consistent with the 3/pi^2 limit. The chi_q (apex) correction is the BIAS,
   not the sign -- the difficulty is in the CAP comparison, where the prime-thin margin bites.
